silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_01_polynomial_form_concrete_anchor a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "PolynomialFormConcreteAnchorExample" .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_01_polynomial_form_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'PolynomialFormConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, VetRecord_77: the concrete carrier set element used to instantiate the polynomial functor; Sigma(VetRecord_77) = four tagged copies (ingest, type, validate, render) of VetRecord_77; also, FourCopyVetRecord: the concrete result of Sigma(VetRecord_77) = VetRecord_77_{ingest} + VetRecord_77_{type} + VetRecord_77_{validate} + VetRecord_77_{render}; four disjoint tagged copies representing VetRecord_77 at each publish stage." .
